From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:15:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/27] tests: batched range-proof and sum checks give the
 single-check verdicts

rct_batch_gates checks that verRctSemanticsSimple over a batch rejects
whatever it rejects for one transaction alone. The block path batches a
block's BP+ proofs and sum checks, and splits them into sub-batches over
the thread pool; batch verifiers in other projects have accepted bad
proofs that their single checks rejected.

- one bad BP+ proof at every position of 64, in batches of 8 to 64 and
  rotated to the front and the back;
- one broken sum: a fee tamper at every position of 33, an output-mask
  tamper at 3 positions of 17;
- nine mutations of a valid proof (L and R swapped, reversed, cut short
  or extended; A and A1 swapped; r1, s1 or d1 zeroed; V spliced from
  another proof) at every position of 8 and 17;
- duplicated proofs, and one batch verified 20 times.

About 70 s of unit_tests time with the next file.

Written by the second reviewer; adopted here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
